      "text": "Step2: Business Intelligence:\r\nBI tools process and present this data as reports, dashboards, charts and \r\nKPIs.\r\nFor example, the manager sees:\r\nSales Dashboard\r\nTotal Sales = \u20b917 lakh\r\nBest-selling product = Laptop\r\nHighest-sales city = Mumbai\r\nSales increased by 20% this month\r\nThis is Business Intelligence.\r\nBI answers: \"What is happening?\"\r\nStep 3: Analytical Decision Making\r\nNow the manager analyzes the information and makes a business decision.\r\nFor example:\r\n\"Laptop sales are highest in Mumbai, and sales have increased by 20%. \r\nTherefore, we should increase laptop inventory in Mumbai and run more laptop \r\nadvertisements there.\"\r\nThis is Analytical Decision Making.\r\nAnalytical decision making answers:\r\n\"What should we do based on the data?\"\r\nBusiness Intelligence: \"What is happening in the business?\"\r\nAnalytical Decision Making: \"What decision should we take based on what the \r\ndata tells us?\"",
